# CraftScript Dashboard Design System

This repo is the **DeFi dashboard** (`app.craftscript.com`). The marketing/landing site lives in `cs_nextjs_client` and has its own layout. Shared brand tokens and grid philosophy apply to both.

## Grid system

| Breakpoint | Columns |
|------------|---------|
| Mobile (`< 768px`) | **4** |
| Desktop (`≥ 768px`) | **7** |

### Rules

- Grids are **full viewport width** — no `max-width` container.
- Header, sidebar, and main content share the same **7-column** desktop grid.
- Grid lines / dividers use `--main-border-color` (`#d4d4d3`).

### Desktop column map

| Element | Column |
|---------|--------|
| Logo (header) | 1 |
| Sidebar | 1 |
| Vertical divider | border on sidebar col 1, or col 2 |
| Main content (router) | 2–7 |
| Connect Wallet (header) | 6–7 |

### Mobile column map

| Element | Column |
|---------|--------|
| Logo | 1 |
| Connect Wallet | 3 |
| Bottom nav items | 4 equal columns |

## Chrome heights

- Header: **64px** (`4rem`) — `--shell-header-height`
- Mobile bottom nav: same height as header
- Scrollable content: `calc(100vh - var(--shell-header-height))`

## Color palette

Defined in `src/assets/styles/default-theme-colors.css`.

| Token | Hex | Usage |
|-------|-----|--------|
| `--primary-text-color` / orange | `#FE6C00` | CTAs, links, accents, active states |
| `--main-bg-color` / black | `#171c1f` | Shell and page background |
| `--main-border-color` | `#d4d4d3` | Grid lines, shell dividers |
| `--gray-30` | `#CFCBD2` | Decorative text, secondary lines |
| `--gray-100` | `#080708` | Body text on light contexts |
| `--main-text-color` / white | `#fff` | Primary text on dark backgrounds |

**Pattern:** dark gray/black base + orange highlights.

Exchange page panel borders (`--exchange-line`) may be darker than shell grid lines — that is intentional.

## Dashboard CTAs

- **Connect Wallet** in the header uses a bordered/filled Material button — correct for this app.
- Marketing **Launch App** is a plain orange text link — do not apply that pattern here.

## Exchange page

- Scope all exchange-specific styles under `.exchange-page` in `src/styles/exchange-page.scss`.
- Reuse shell tokens (`--primary-text-color`, `--main-bg-color`) — do not introduce alternate orange/background hex values.
- Do not leak exchange styles into global shell components.

## Reference files

- `src/assets/styles/default-theme-colors.css` — color tokens
- `src/styles.scss` — shell tokens (`--shell-header-height`, grid columns)
- `src/app/components/layout/` — app frame grid
- `src/app/components/header/` — logo + wallet placement
- `src/app/components/sidebar/` — navigation
- `src/styles/exchange-page.scss` — Token Exchange page
- `docs/design-system.md` — human-readable summary
- `cs_nextjs_client/docs/design-system.md` — marketing site details

## Agent checklist for layout/styling changes

1. Keep header at exactly `4rem` including bottom border — no overflow from separate line elements.
2. Sidebar width must equal header column 1 (`1/7` viewport on desktop).
3. Use CSS variables for orange and background — never hardcode `#ff6900` or `#111719`.
4. Preserve wallet MFE integration and exchange page class structure.
5. Run `pnpm run lint` and `pnpm run build` before finishing.
6. Run `pnpm run e2e` when changing shell layout, header, sidebar, or grid chrome.
